  "notes": [
    "Section totals and numbered-question mark pattern follow the official sample paper: Biology 30, Chemistry 25, Physics 25; 20×1 mark, 6×2 marks, 7×3 marks, 3×4 marks and 3×5 marks.",
    "Internal-choice slots are questions 11, 15, 16, 26, 28, 29, 34, 38 and 39. Alternative options carry the same total marks as the main option.",
    "CBSE specifies aggregate theory competency weighting of 50% knowledge and understanding, 30% application, and 20% analysis/evaluation/creation. Slot-level primary competency tags are ExamGuru's allocation to meet those aggregate mark targets; CBSE does not prescribe fixed competency labels per numbered question.",
    "Annual-examination unit weights of 25, 25, 12, 13 and 5 marks are enforced for every generated paper.",
    "Syllabus discrepancy: the official sample paper includes heredity-style question content, while the 2026–27 curriculum says Heredity and Evolution are formative-only and not assessed in the year-end examination. ExamGuru's pool excludes Heredity and Evolution pending clarification.",
    "The question pool contains original ExamGuru-authored practice questions, not copied CBSE sample-paper questions. The official sample paper is used for structural verification only.",
    "Formative-only topics excluded from summative authoring include Periodic Classification of Elements; Heredity and Evolution; and Motor, Electromagnetic Induction and Electric Generator.",
    "Question form is mapped to the published numbered paper: Q1–7 MCQ; Q8–9 assertion–reason; Q10–13 structured response; Q14 data/food-chain case; Q15 structured response (ExamGuru replaces the formative-only heredity item with summative syllabus content); Q16 diagram-based; Q17–23 MCQ; Q24 assertion–reason; Q25–27 structured response; Q28–29 case/experimental reasoning; Q30–31 MCQ; Q32 assertion–reason; Q33–34 structured response; Q35 numerical; Q36 structured response; Q37 circuit-diagram numerical; Q38 case-based; Q39 diagram-based."
  ]
